                        "sense_id": "985a809d-60ce-3856-b8e2-5598179af6e6",
                        "entry_id": "3c4c2026-4ef6-397a-a07d-f57549463924",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a perverse manner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9be8b57-4c5a-4620-b768-796d31c52800",
                                "sense_id": "985a809d-60ce-3856-b8e2-5598179af6e6",
                                "text": "But even if one of the curves is sloped “perversely,” the condition may still be fulfilled […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a418d3b-85c7-41b1-aa49-038ebd03fdec",
                                "sense_id": "985a809d-60ce-3856-b8e2-5598179af6e6",
                                "text": "By such perversely exacting standards the possibilities for a genuine, living Inuit art to exist at all are slim."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "85993fda-60ae-4581-9e97-c60403457b3b",
                                "sense_id": "985a809d-60ce-3856-b8e2-5598179af6e6",
                                "text": "There is another reason the films are so entertaining and successful, though (with the franchise earning more than $500 million dollars so far). Perversely, we love John Wick himself. That lethal, bereaved assassin is a good bad guy for our times, the natural extension of Tony Soprano, Walter White and all the other heroic antiheroes the culture has embraced."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
